Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1789991999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["30 of the last 33 bars are a two-sided 2357.18-2700 range with heavy overlap; the 2771 spike high made 30 bars ago is still the window high, so trend continuation is not confirmed.", "Bar 89 closed below the midpoint of its 445.69 range (buy climax), and the 2609.02-2700 area has now rejected upside probes three times (bar 113 close 2514.07 area, bar 110 high 2680 closed 2514.72, bar 118 high 2700 closed 2632.98 in the lower third of its range).", "The 120-bar window contains a full 36% bear leg (2116.86 to 1368.42) in its first 14 bars, so the window is not a single clean bull trend and the bear-trend context is only 100 bars old.", "No bar closes above 2700 yet: bar 118 leaves an upper tail and bar 119 is an inside bar, so the current push is still a boundary test, and repeated boundary tests in a range often resolve either way."], "evidence_for": ["Swing progression since the 1368.42 low is higher lows (1512.91 bar 33, 1512.91 -> 2357.18/2358.62 bars 101/114) and higher highs (1845.09, 1954.36, 1974.46, 2771), which is a bull sequence at the window level.", "The bar 87-89 spike closed far above the 24-bar 1821.49-1974.46 range and the following 30 bars never traded back below 2293.80 (bar 87 high), so the breakout was accepted rather than reversed: the range/base is left behind.", "The window's three highest closes are the last three bars (2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90), and bar 119 closes near the top of its range at 2642.90, showing buyers still pressing at the range top at the decision time.", "Lows inside the post-spike range rise after bar 101 (2374.01, 2411.04, 2413.82, 2436.87, 2568.16), a mild upward tilt consistent with a bull flag rather than a topping structure."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Bars 0-13 are a bear leg: window opens 2116.86, high 2139.34 (bar 1), low 1368.42 (bar 13), about -36% from the high.", "Bar 13 (open 1581.32, high 1599.27, low 1368.42, close 1568.55) closes 200.13 above its low, near the top of its 230.85 range: the leg ends in a climactic reversal bar rather than a trend-continuation close.", "After 1368.42 the market rallies to 1845.09 (bar 22 high) and then pulls back to 1512.91 (bar 33 low), a higher low; the subsequent leg reaches 1954.36 (bar 59 high) and 1974.46 (bar 64 high).", "Bars 63-86 are a 24-bar range between 1974.46 (bar 64 high) and 1821.49 (bar 71 low); bar 63 prints 1959.37, just above bar 59's 1954.36, and bar 64 immediately reverses to close 1891.41 near its low (failed breakout/upthrust).", "Bar 87 opens 1916.51 inside that range and closes 2252.16 (high 2293.80, low 1905.63), a +17.5% close-to-close bull bar; bar 88 closes 2326.32 and bar 89 reaches 2771.", "Bar 89 (open 2326.31, high 2771, low 2325.31, close 2515.30) closes below the midpoint 2548.16 of its 445.69 range: a long upper tail, and the 2771 high has not been exceeded in the following 30 bars.", "Bars 90-119 trade between 2357.18 (bar 101 low) and 2700 (bar 118 high) with heavy overlap and never return below 2293.80 (bar 87 high): the breakout zone 1821.49-1974.46 is left behind.", "Upside probes at 2680 (bar 110 high, close 2514.72) and 2700 (bar 118 high, close 2632.98, i.e. the lower third of its 2604.75-2700 range) both closed back inside the 30-bar range.", "Bar 114 sells to 2358.62 and closes 2397.10; the next five closes rise: 2416.57, 2446.22, 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90. Those last three are the three highest closes of the whole 120-bar window (next highest is 2515.30 on bar 89).", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is an inside bar versus bar 118 and closes 57.10 below the 2700 high, near the top of its own range."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear leg of the window ending in a climactic bar: 2116.86 open, high 2139.34 (bar 1), low 1368.42 (bar 13). Bar 13 is a bear bar closing 200.13 above its low in the upper part of its range, the exhaustion bar of the leg.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779580800000, "upper_boundary": "2139.34"}, {"description": "Mid-window trading range, 24 bars (63-86) confined between 1974.46 (bar 64 high) and 1821.49 (bar 71 low), width 152.97 (about 8%). Bar 63 marginally exceeds the prior swing high 1954.36 and bar 64 reverses to close 1891.41 near its low: a failed breakout above the prior high.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1821.49", "start_time_ms": 1785024000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the 24-bar range: bar 87 opens 1916.51 inside the range and closes 2252.16 (high 2293.80, low 1905.63); bars 88 (close 2326.32) and 89 (open 2326.31, high 2771, close 2515.30) extend it. Bar 89 closes below the midpoint of its 445.69 range (long upper tail), so the third bar is climactic.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Post-spike trading range, 30 bars (90-119): overlapping two-sided trade between 2357.18 (bar 101 low) and 2700 (bar 118 high), never returning below 2293.80 (bar 87 high). Spike highs at 2680 (bar 110) and 2700 (bar 118) were both sold back into the range; lows after bar 101 rise from 2374.01 (bar 102) to 2568.16 (bar 119) with one near-retest at 2358.62 (bar 114).", "end_time_ms": 1789948799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Recent bull leg off bar 114's low 2358.62: five rising closes 2416.57, 2446.22, 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, the highest closes of the window. Bar 117 closes 2612.02 near its 2643.52 high; bar 119 is an inside bar versus bar 118 and closes 2642.90, 57.10 under the 2700 range top. Still a leg inside the 30-bar range, not an accepted breakout.", "end_time_ms": 1789948799999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789430400000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["A daily close above 2700 (bar 118 high) with a further bull close would mark acceptance of an upside breakout from the 30-bar range and support continued bull-trend/channel behaviour.", "A bear close below 2568.16 (bar 119 low) followed by a break of 2357.18 (bar 101 low) would break the 30-bar range low and shift the read toward a lower high under 2771 and a range-down resolution.", "Continuation of overlapping bars contained inside 2436.87 (bar 117 low) and 2700 keeps the phase 'range' and keeps always-in relevance low.", "A move back below 2293.80 (bar 87 high, the top of the breakout bar's range) would undercut breakout acceptance and move the classification toward transition-unclear."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789977599999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Both earlier bull spikes in this window were fully retraced, so a spike here has not historically produced a sustained trend: 1788436800000 (high 2509.15) gave way to 2436.73 at 1788523200000, and 1789128000000 (high 2680.00) gave way to 2358.62 at 1789488000000, below its own origin.", "The last fifteen bars are two-sided overlap inside 2568.16-2700.00 with small bodies (for example 1789819200000 open 2638.59/close 2640.01, 1789833600000 open 2640.01/close 2633.54, 1789848000000 open 2633.54/close 2632.98) and no new trend bar, which is range-like rather than channel-like.", "2700.00 was rejected twice with upper tails on the same bars that printed it: 1789804800000 closed 61.51 below its high and 1789948800000 closed 35.27 below its high, an exact double top at a round number.", "Three consecutive closes (2586.68, 2576.9, 2577.88 at 1789862400000-1789891200000) fell back below the 2609.02 breakout level, so acceptance above the old range top is not clean.", "A large part of the sample is two-sided overlap: bars 1788537600000-1789718400000 (67 bars) repeatedly reversed between roughly 2400 and 2610, so the directional leg covers a minority of the window."], "evidence_for": ["Since the 1789488000000 low of 2358.62 the sequence of swing lows is rising: about 2370.54 (1789574400000), 2436.87 (1789689600000), 2568.16 (1789891200000), while highs rise 2481.66 (1789646400000), 2643.52 (1789761600000), 2700.00 (1789948800000).", "The 1789732800000 and 1789761600000 bars are consecutive large trend bars closing at/near their highs (close 2578.6 vs high 2585.5; close 2636.28 vs high 2643.52) and they broke above the 2609.02 high of 1789416000000.", "Acceptance is visible on closes: 12 of the 15 closes after 1789761600000 are above 2609.02, and the market has not traded back into the middle of the old 2357-2610 range.", "The final four bars are bull bars with closes in the upper part of their ranges (2611.00, 2631.93, 2642.90, 2664.73), restoring the up leg after the 1789862400000-1789891200000 pullback.", "The window's upper extremes progress upward across the sample: 2537.57 (1788508800000), 2609.02 (1789416000000), 2680.00 (1789128000000), 2700.00 (1789948800000)."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Supplied window is 120 closed H4 bars, 1788249600000 to 1789977599999; first close 2468.97, last close 2658.81, net +189.84.", "Window low 2357.18 (1788278400000 bar low); window high 2700.00 printed twice, on 1789804800000 (open 2626.53, close 2638.49) and 1789948800000 (open 2642.9, close 2664.73).", "Three outsized bull bars: 1788436800000 (open 2407.48, high 2509.15, close 2506.79), 1789128000000 (open 2457.12, high 2680.00, close 2555.52), and the pair 1789732800000/1789761600000 (opens 2507.15/2579.97, highs 2585.5/2643.52, closes 2578.6/2636.28, each closing 6.9 and 7.24 below its high).", "The fifteen bars from 1789761600000 to 1789977599999 overlap inside 2568.16 (1789891200000 low) and 2700.00: closes 2612.02, 2619.15, 2626.53, 2638.49, 2640.01, 2633.54, 2632.98, 2586.68, 2576.9, 2577.88, 2611.00, 2631.93, 2642.9, 2664.73, 2658.81.", "Last four bars (1789905600000-1789948800000) close higher each time (2611.00, 2631.93, 2642.90, 2664.73) after the 1789891200000 low of 2568.16; the final bar (1789963200000) opens 2664.73, high 2674.67, low 2646.02, close 2658.81, a small bear bar 5.92 below its open and 41.19 below the 2700.00 high.", "Repeated tests of the same zone: highs 2607.62 (1789142400000) and 2609.02 (1789416000000) above; lows 2357.18 (1788336000000) and 2358.62 (1789488000000) below."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Two-sided range dominating the middle of the window: alternating spikes and full retracements between the 2357.18 low (1788336000000) and the 2680.00 high (1789128000000), with overlapping bodies and many reversals. The 1788436800000 bull spike (close 2506.79) was retraced to 2436.73 at 1788523200000, and the 1789128000000 bull spike (close 2555.52) was retraced all the way to 2358.62 at 1789488000000, below its own origin.", "end_time_ms": 1789718400000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1788321600000, "upper_boundary": "2680.00"}, {"description": "Bull breakout above the 2609.02 high of 1789416000000 (a level corroborated by the 2607.62 high of 1789142400000): the 1789732800000/1789761600000 trend bars (closes 2578.6/2636.28) cleared it and 12 of the 15 closes since sit above it. 2700.00 was reached at 1789804800000 and again at 1789948800000. Caveat within the structure: the 1789862400000-1789891200000 pullback closed back below the level on three consecutive bars (2586.68, 2576.9, 2577.88) before recovering.", "end_time_ms": 1789977599999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2609.02", "start_time_ms": 1789732800000, "upper_boundary": "2700.00"}, {"description": "Rising, overlapping progression from the 2358.62 low (1789488000000): higher swing lows near 2370.54 (1789574400000), 2436.87 (1789689600000) and 2568.16 (1789891200000), against higher highs 2481.66 (1789646400000), 2643.52 (1789761600000) and 2700.00 (1789948800000), with each push separated by two-sided pullback bars.", "end_time_ms": 1789977599999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2700.00"}, {"description": "The fifteen bars from 1789761600000 to 1789977599999 overlap inside 2568.16-2700.00: three bear bars at 1789862400000-1789891200000 erased much of the 1789761600000 advance, a 2700.00 double top formed with upper tails of 61.51 and 35.27 points, and no new trend bar appeared.", "end_time_ms": 1789977599999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2568.16", "start_time_ms": 1789761600000, "upper_boundary": "2700.00"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2700.00 followed by a bar that holds above it would confirm the breakout and extend the bull channel.", "A close below 2568.16 (the 1789891200000 low) would break the higher-low sequence and shift the read toward trading-range/range.", "Continued overlapping bars between 2568.16 and 2700.00 with shrinking ranges would convert the current channel into a trading range at the highs (phase range).", "Repeated closes back below 2609.02 would mark the breakout as failed and re-establish the wide 2357.18-2680.00 range as the operative structure.", "A single large bear trend bar closing near its low and below 2609.02 would make the Always-In direction ambiguous rather than long."], "window